                        {
                            "id": "SuspiciousIndentation",
                            "shortDescription": {
                                "text": "Suspicious indentation"
                            },
                            "fullDescription": {
                                "text": "This check looks for cases where the indentation suggests a grouping that isn't actually there in the code. A common example of this would be something like\nif (column > width)\n    line++\n    column = 0\nHere, the column = 0 line will be executed every single time, not just if the condition is true.",
                                "markdown": "This check looks for cases where the indentation suggests a grouping that isn't actually there in the code. A common example of this would be something like\n```kotlin\nif (column > width)\n    line++\n    column = 0\n```\nHere, the `column = 0` line will be executed every single time, not just if the condition is true."
